        itemId = 44160,
        name = "Red Proto-Drake",
        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 14,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Complete the Heroic dungeon challenge meta, including controlled mechanics and repeated daily visits.\n\n1. Track Glory of the Hero and its unfinished criteria. Use a strong Retail character, but bring a way to reduce damage for mechanics that need a living boss: unequip weapons and proc gear, disable pets, and consider Whole-Body Shrinka' if you own it. Check every criterion before killing its boss, because Heroic bosses save you for the day.\n\n2. Utgarde Keep, lower entrance in Howling Fjord (58.2, 48.9): kill Prince Keleseth without shattering a Frost Tomb for On The Rocks. A fast single-target kill avoids the tomb mechanic entirely.\n\n3. The Nexus, bottom Nexus portal in Coldarra (27.5, 26.2): kill Keristrasza before Intense Cold exceeds two stacks, moving or jumping if the fight lasts. Kill Telestra quickly, or kill all split images within five seconds of one another. Kill Anomalus without destroying any Chaotic Rifts.\n\n4. Azjol-Nerub, Dragonblight (26.0, 50.6): kill Krik'thir while Gashra, Narji, and Silthik remain alive; use single-target damage. Reach and kill Hadronox before the top doors are webbed. Kill Anub'arak within four minutes, including any scripted underground phases.\n\n5. Ahn'kahet, the other Azjol-Nerub complex entrance (28.3, 51.6): kill Nadox without killing an Ahn'kahar Guardian, finish Volazj within two minutes, and defeat Jedoga without killing a Twilight Volunteer. If you do not kill Jedoga immediately, allow her chosen volunteer to finish its sacrifice.\n\n6. Drak'Tharon Keep, southern Zul'Drak approach (28.6, 86.9): kill Trollgore before ten Consume stacks. At Novos, intercept the undead and Crystal Handlers on the stairs before any reach the floor. Pull King Dred, kill six eligible raptor adds while he is engaged, then finish him; killing the raptors first does not count.\n\n7. Original Violet Hold, Northrend Dalaran (67.9, 69.4): finish with full prison integrity and without using Defense Control Crystals for Defenseless. Kill Ichoron before globules merge, and Zuramat without killing Void Sentries. For Lockdown!, defeat all six listed random prison bosses over multiple Heroic visits; each run releases only two of them.\n\n8. Gundrak, Zul'Drak (76.3, 21.1): kill Slad'ran before being snake-wrapped and Moorabi before any mammoth transformation. After the western boss, take the side passage to Eck, wait for his spit to apply Eck Residue, and retain that debuff until Gal'darah dies. Activate the main-boss altars to open the final route. Do not cleanse the residue or die before the final boss.\n\n9. Halls of Stone, western Ulduar dungeon approach: defeat the Maiden within the Good Grief timer. Protect Brann throughout the Tribunal event so he takes no damage. At Sjonnir, reduce his health carefully to around half, stop attacking him, let Malformed Oozes merge, kill five Iron Sludges during the encounter, then finish Sjonnir.\n\n10. Halls of Lightning, eastern Ulduar dungeon approach: wait until General Bjarngrim visibly has Temporary Electrical Charge before killing him. Kill Volkhan before he shatters any Brittle Golems, and kill Loken within two minutes. Do not pull Bjarngrim during his uncharged patrol just because he is easy to kill.\n\n11. Heroic Culling of Stratholme, Caverns of Time: begin Chromie's crate sequence and Arthas's event. For Zombiefest!, gather at least 100 Risen Zombies without killing them, allowing respawns before Salramm dies, then kill 100 within one minute. Remove all passive area damage. Separately reach the optional Infinite Corruptor before the 25-minute timer ends for The Culling of Time; follow the side path at the final Market Row approach before Mal'Ganis.\n\n12. Utgarde Pinnacle, upper Howling Fjord entrance (57.3, 46.7): for The Incredible Hulk, keep a Scourge Hulk alive, weaken it with controlled damage, and position it beneath Svala's ritual sword so her strike kills it. Do not kill either target early. For Skadi, collect three Harpoons and fire them in one pass, then finish him within three minutes. Kill Ymiron without triggering Bane; a fast kill avoids it.\n\n13. The Oculus, middle Nexus ring: plan three Heroic completions on the same character, riding a different drake color for each Eregos kill. Finish within 20 minutes of Drakos for Make It Count. The Void achievements mean WITHOUT that color: a solo Ruby clear excludes Amber and Emerald, and a solo Amber or Emerald clear excludes Ruby. For Amber, build Temporal Rift charges and spend them with Shock Lance, using Stop Time; for Emerald, maintain Leeching Poison and use its healing/damage tools. Bring help using the same chosen color if a solo vehicle kill is difficult.\n\n14. Reopen Glory of the Hero, finish any missing random-boss or drake-color criteria after the appropriate daily resets, then check your mailbox for Reins of the Red Proto-Drake. Use the reins. The three Icecrown five-player dungeons and Trial of the Champion are not part of this original dungeon meta.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=44160",
        difficultyReason = "Complete the Heroic dungeon challenge meta, including controlled mechanics and repeated daily visits.",
        difficulty = "hard",
    },
    [59996] = {
