        itemId = 44168,
        name = "Time-Lost Proto-Drake",
        mountCategory = "Rare Drops",
        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Search a contested rare-spawn route with a long, unpredictable timer shared with Vyragosa.\n\n1. Travel to the Storm Peaks in Northrend and choose the same phase and War Mode setting as anyone camping with you. Use a ground-accessible pull spot or prepare a way to land safely; the rare patrols in the air.\n\n2. Cover the western Bor's Breath/waterfall area near 31.0, 69.0. Watch the canyon and the air above it. The Time-Lost Proto-Drake is gold-brown; the much more common blue rare Vyragosa is not the mount source.\n\n3. Cover the southern Frozen Lake/Frosthold approach near 35.0, 76.0. If camping in a small party, assign different search areas and communicate sightings before attacking.\n\n4. Check the Brunnhildar route near 51.0, 70.0 and the northern Ulduar-ravine route near 52.0, 34.0. Fly between the marked areas if searching alone. A single coordinate cannot cover every patrol path.\n\n5. When the actual Time-Lost Proto-Drake appears, check that its nameplate is loot-eligible for you before killing it. For a group attempt, gather nearby and arrange participation before using an attack that can instantly kill this old rare. Do not assume a distant party member will receive loot.\n\n6. Bring it over safe ground where possible, kill it, loot Reins of the Time-Lost Proto-Drake, and learn the mount. The reins are guaranteed from a loot-eligible kill; the uncertain part is finding and tagging the rare.\n\n7. If you find Vyragosa instead, killing her frees the shared spawn cycle for a future spawn, but does not guarantee that the next one is Time-Lost. Record sightings if helpful and return without relying on old item-cache macros or a promised weekly appearance.",
