        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Build the usable-mount collection through ordinary vendors and deterministic rewards.\n\n1. Track Leading the Cavalry in the achievement window and note its current counter. The target is 50 mounts usable by an eligible character. For the dragonhawks, use an Alliance character for Blue and a Horde character for Red when checking the reward.\n\n2. Start with inexpensive racial mounts you have not learned. Use a character of the matching original race, or earn the vendor's home-city reputation to Exalted. Buy every uncollected ordinary and swift color you qualify for; each distinct learned mount adds collection progress.\n\n3. Add missing basic and swift gryphon or wind-rider colors from the flying-mount vendors in your faction capital. Then visit Mei Francis in Northrend Dalaran (57.8, 42.5) for any uncollected gold mounts within your budget. Check the journal before buying faction counterparts twice.\n\n4. For a reliable additional group, unlock Netherwing at the Netherwing Fields in Outland Shadowmoon Valley (59.3, 58.7), complete its reputation quests to Exalted, and collect all six drake colors. Another option is the Mag'har/Kurenai talbuk group in Nagrand: its Exalted vendor sells multiple distinct riding and war colors.\n\n5. After each group of purchases, use every item and recheck the tracked achievement. At 50, log onto an eligible character and check both the journal and mailbox for Albino Drake. If the displayed total is short, compare your usable-mount counter before buying an expensive extra mount.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=44178",
        difficultyReason = "Build the usable-mount collection through ordinary vendors and deterministic rewards.",
        difficulty = "medium",
    },
