                step = 2,
                label = "High Seat - defeat all three council members",
                mapName = "Ironforge",
            },
            {
                mapID = 62,
                x = 0.489,
                y = 0.245,
                step = 3,
                label = "Zidormi - optional pre-burning travel phase",
                mapName = "Darkshore",
            },
            { mapID = 103, x = 0.325, y = 0.545, step = 4, label = "Prophet Velen - Vault of Lights", mapName = "The Exodar" },
        },
        itemId = 44224,
        name = "Black War Bear",
        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Defeat current enemy-faction leaders with a suitable group and account for city defenses and PvP interference.\n\n1. On a Horde character, track For the Horde! and inspect the live criteria. The current Retail page lists Overthrow the Council and Putting Out the Light. Form a same-faction group with a tank and healer, choose matching War Mode settings, and enter each city together.\n\n2. Go to the High Seat in Ironforge (39.6, 56.0). Defeat all three Council of Three Hammers members: Muradin Bronzebeard, Moira Thaurissan, and Falstad Wildhammer. Keep the group in credit range and verify Overthrow the Council before leaving.\n\n3. Reach Azuremyst Isle and enter the Exodar. A practical Horde approach is through pre-burning Darkshore and Rut'theran's Azuremyst connection; use Zidormi at Darkshore (48.9, 24.5) if the route is hidden by the burned phase. A warlock already on Azuremyst can also summon the group.\n\n4. In the Exodar, reach Prophet Velen in the Vault of Lights (32.5, 54.5). Control the guards, interrupt healing where possible, and defeat Velen for Putting Out the Light. Verify the achievement before the group disperses.\n\n5. Check For the Horde! for completion, then inspect the Mount Journal and mailbox for the Horde Black War Bear. If your game lists an additional criterion, follow that live requirement; do not repeat a four-city Wrath-era itinerary by default.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=44224",
        difficultyReason = "Defeat current enemy-faction leaders with a suitable group and account for city defenses and PvP interference.",
        difficulty = "hard",
